[[File:Shopkeeper I AM ERROR.png|120px]]

The {{r|I AM ERROR}} room is a rare room that isn't connected to any other room on the floor and is reached through glitches or as a failsafe for an impossible event (like using {{i|Blank Card}} on {{p|? Card}}, which loops on itself infinitely without a failsafe).

'''I AM ERROR''' rooms are chaotic and often contain multiple items, pickups, beggars, and/or powerful enemies. There are no doors to leave, but always an exit to the next level ({{dlc|r}} with few exceptions) and at least one unique shopkeeper (pictured above) with a text bubble that reads "I AM ERROR".

The trapdoor will always be open, even if there are enemies in the room.

== Accessing the I AM ERROR room ==
* The only items/effects that can bring Isaac to the I AM ERROR room are [[Telepills]], {{i|Undefined}}, {{i|Teleport 2.0}}, {{i|Red Key}} and {{i|Blank Card}} + {{p|? Card}}. (This '''<u>consumes</u>''' {{i|Blank Card}} and {{p|? Card}})
* {{i|Undefined}} is the simplest method, as it has a decent chance to teleport the player there.
* {{dlc+|r}} Using {{i|Red Key}} on the 13x13 boundaries of the map will create a 1-way door to the I AM ERROR room, and displays no icon on the map upon opening.
** No red door outlines will appear on the normal floor's boundary walls, meaning the I AM ERROR room can only be entered from another {{r|Red Room}}. At least 2 uses of {{P|Cracked Key}} are needed to enter if you don't have access to {{i|Red Key}}.
** Doesn't work on the {{s|Chest}}, {{s|Dark Room}}, {{s|The Void}}, {{s|Home}}, {{s|Corpse}} II, or the {{i|Dad's Note}} floor.{{dlc-}}
* {{dlc+|a}} Using {{i|Teleport 2.0}} when all rooms on the floor have been explored (including the {{r|Secret Room}}(s), {{r|Super Secret Room}}(s), and the {{r|Devil Room}} or {{r|Angel Room}}) sends you to the I AM ERROR room.{{dlc-}}
* {{dlc+|r}} The I AM ERROR room can be reached by leaving a {{r|Crawl Space}} through an unintended direction. This will '''<u>always</u>''' bring you to an error room, even when all other methods stop working.
** {{i|Blank Card}} + {{p|XXI - The World?|n}}, {{I|Clear Rune}} + {{P|Ehwaz}}, {{I|We Need To Go Deeper!}}, and {{I|Mom's Shovel}} offer consistent methods of creating crawl spaces.
** Use 4 size downs, 2 speed, and crash into the floor below the entrance ladder ''or'' 3 size downs and the left and right walls using flight.
*** [[Pills|One makes you smaller]] is the easiest way to acquire multiple size downs, and although you can exit the crawl space using listed minimums, it sometimes requires a lot of patience. {{I|Pluto}} / {{I|Inner Child}} are equal to 4 uses of the pill.
*** It is also possible to exit through an unintended direction using {{I|A Pony}} / {{I|White Pony}} and 1 size down, albeit rarely. Significantly more common with 2 or more size downs. The speed stat does not matter since the charge-speed is a flat velocity.
*** You can use {{I|Spin to Win}}, 2 speed & flight just by themselves to exit, bouncing off the far left and right walls and timing turning around after each bounce to build up speed and eventually exit.
*** {{c|Tainted Forgotten}} can be thrown outside the {{r|Crawl Space}} provided {{c|Tainted Soul}} builds up enough velocity, resulting in accessing the I AM ERROR room.
*** {{c|The Forgotten}} can place his body at the bottom of the entrance ladder, swap to the Soul form, then stretch vertically towards the entrance. Slingshotting yourself downward using the chain can provide some extra speed in order to clip. {{dlc-}}
* {{dlc|r+}} A trapdoor created in the {{i|Lil Portal|n}} bedroom with {{i|We Need To Go Deeper!}} or {{p|Ehwaz}} will always lead to the I AM ERROR room.

== I AM ERROR room destination ==
* Entering the I AM ERROR room from {{S|Womb}} II, {{S|Utero}} II, {{S|Scarred Womb}} II or {{S|???}} will randomly result in a trapdoor or a beam of light. Isaac may have to end his run early in the {{S|Cathedral}}/{{S|Sheol}} if the wrong story item was collected.
* {{dlc+|r}} The second part of each Alt floor shall send Isaac back to the main route. (for example, {{s|Downpour}} II's trapdoor goes to Caves II.){{dlc-}}
* {{dlc+|r}} The only way to access the I AM ERROR room on {{s|Chest}}, {{s|Dark Room}}, {{s|The Void}}, {{s|Home}}, {{s|Corpse}} II, or the {{i|Dad's Note}} floor is through glitching out of bounds inside of a {{r|Crawl Space}}. Methods such as {{i|Teleport 2.0}} will instead create an I am Error Shopkeeper.
** {{s|Chest}} and {{s|Dark Room}}'s I AM ERROR room contain a portal to {{s|The Void}}.
*** If {{s|The Void}} is not unlocked, it will instead contain a trapdoor that brings Isaac back to the floor.
** {{s|Corpse}} II, {{s|Home}}, {{s|The Void}}, and the {{i|Dad's Note}} floor all have I AM ERROR room which contains a trapdoor that puts Isaac back onto the floor.
*** {{dlc|nr+}} In the rare event of accessing I AM ERROR on {{s|Corpse}} XL and encountering a trapdoor in that error room, Isaac is taken to a new floor which attempts to load then the game crashes.
*** {{dlc|r+}} Entering the I AM ERROR room in {{S|Corpse}} XL will create a trapodoor or a beam of light that sends Isaac to {{S|Cathedral}} or {{S|Sheol}}, similarly to {{S|Womb}} II, {{S|Utero}} II, {{S|Scarred Womb}} II or {{S|???}}.
**** This can be viewed by enabling the LABY RNTH seed and getting into the Corpse XL Error room.{{dlc-}}
* {{dlc|na+}} Entering the exit of an I AM ERROR room in the {{s|Chest}} or {{s|Dark Room}} will restart the floor.
* {{dlc|a+nr}} The I AM ERROR room cannot be reached in {{s|Chest}}, {{s|Dark Room}}, or the final floor of the [[daily challenge]].
* {{dlc|r}} During the [[Ascent]], the I AM ERROR room will contain a beam of light instead.

