== Notes ==
* Once Isaac arrives at the I AM ERROR room, the only ways out are the trapdoor to the next level or another teleport. As the I AM ERROR room is randomly reached, this could force Isaac to skip {{r|Treasure Room}} and/or {{r|Boss Room}} items if they hadn't been picked up before, and if he cannot teleport again.
* Items in the I AM ERROR room will be from random [[item pool]]s.
* {{dlc+|r}} Once [[Corrupted Data]] is achieved (beating {{e|Delirium}} as {{c|Tainted Eden}}), items that spawn in this room have a 1/16 chance to be randomized as if affected by {{i|TMTRAINER}}.{{dlc-}}
* If a {{r|Crawl Space}} is spawned in the I AM ERROR room, Isaac will return to the room he was in before being teleported to the I AM ERROR room upon exiting the Crawl Space.
* Using the trapdoor in the I AM ERROR room can allow Isaac to reach levels not yet unlocked, like {{S|Sheol}} or {{S|Cathedral}}.
* {{dlc|na}} Using the trapdoor in {{S|Chest}} or the {{S|Dark Room}} will restart the level, similar to the effect of the {{I|Forget Me Now}}, and as of patch 1.05, the floor will generate a different layout upon restarting. The door to {{E|Mega Satan}} will be locked if it was previously opened.
* The chests present in the I AM ERROR room while on {{s|Chest}} and {{s|Dark Room}} always contain items.
* Using the {{P|Jera}} in most of these room configurations can allow Isaac to duplicate a very large amount of pickups, making Jera especially effective in this room.
* If Isaac is teleported to a {{r|Devil Room}} or {{r|Angel Room}} from an I AM ERROR room (e. g. by using {{p|Joker}}), exiting the room will return him to the room he was in ''before'' entering the I AM ERROR room.
* It is probably not a good idea to go to the I AM ERROR room on {{S|Depths}}/{{S|Necropolis}}/{{S|Dank Depths}} II before getting {{i|The Polaroid}}/{{i|The Negative}}, because then you can't go to the {{S|Chest}} or {{S|Dark Room}}, having to end the run in {{S|Sheol}} or {{S|Cathedral}}.
** Reaching another I AM ERROR room in the above-mentioned levels would allow continuing the run beyond them, even lacking the prerequisite items.
** Note that the 12th reward and onward in a {{r|Sacrifice Room}} has a 50% chance to send Isaac to {{S|Dark Room}}. This may be useful if an I AM ERROR room locked Isaac out of {{i|The Negative}}.
** {{dlc+|r}} This rule also applies to Isaac when trying to reach an alternate floor from a main floor ({{S|Downpour}} II from {{S|Basement}} II, etc.). The I AM ERROR room will always send him to a regular floor ({{S|Basement}} II to {{S|Caves}} I, etc.) and Isaac will not be able to pick up the necessary progression items needed to reach {{s|Corpse}}.
*** However, in {{S|Mausoleum}}/{{S|Gehenna}} II, if Isaac kills {{e|Mom's Heart}} first, then enters the I AM ERROR room, the trapdoor inside will lead him to {{S|Corpse}}.{{dlc-}}
* {{dlc|a}} There is a rare [[Closets|Closet]] room in {{S|Depths}} and {{S|Necropolis}} containing an I AM ERROR shopkeeper. This is not an I AM ERROR room, and can be exited normally.
* {{dlc|a}} There is a {{r|Super Secret Room}} that looks like an I AM ERROR room. This is not an I AM ERROR room, and can be exited normally.

== Trivia ==
* The I AM ERROR room is a reference to an infamous quote in the NES game [[wikipedia:Zelda II: The Adventure of Link|''Zelda II: The Adventure of Link'']], where a citizen from Ruto introduces himself with the sentence "[[wikipedia:I am Error|I AM ERROR]]".

